// Logout permitted if the same user logged in within the last hour.
// `Login` has fields `(user, server)`, but the predicate only mentions
// `user` — `server` is omitted. Per the documented "omitted fields are
// implicitly wildcarded" rule, the runtime must match any prior Login
// for `context.input.user` regardless of which `server` it used.
//
// Distinct from 0270 (which exercises trace-field *ordering*), this
// case asserts the *omission* semantics directly: the trace's Login
// and Logout deliberately use different `server` values so that any
// implementation that constrains the predicate by all schema-declared
// fields would fail to match. The expected verdict is permit at the
// Logout time-point.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Logout",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
